# Unity package lock is resolved by the editor; keep if you want reproducible
# bridge pins, ignore if you prefer the manifest ref to drive resolution.
# Packages/packages-lock.json

# Loombridge: ONE rule, and it is structural (Docs/Design/ArtifactStorage.md).
#
# Everything Loombridge re-derives from an anchor plus a run lives under
# .loombridge/run/. Everything else under .loombridge/ is meant to be COMMITTED: the
# contract files, design/, tests/, verify/, registry/, and above all anchors/ (the
# recorded human demonstrations and the approved pixel baselines). An anchor whose
# evidence never leaves one machine is not a gate.
#
# THE TRAILING `*` IS LOAD-BEARING, and `.loombridge/run/` would be a bug. Git cannot
# re-include anything inside an EXCLUDED DIRECTORY, so the directory form would also hide
# .loombridge/run/.gitignore, the marker that makes the run tier ignore itself in a fresh
# clone that has not run a Loombridge verb yet. Measured, not assumed: with the directory
# form `git add .` stages neither the marker nor anything under it; with the `*` form it
# stages the marker and nothing else.
.loombridge/run/*

# Slice checkpoints. OUTSIDE .loombridge/ because snapshotSliceFixture copies the whole
# state dir into this one, and Node refuses to copy a directory into a subdirectory of
# itself (ERR_FS_CP_EINVAL). It can never move inside, so it needs its own rule.
.loombridge-fixtures/

# NOT ignored, on purpose:
#
#   .loombridge/anchors/  the recorded demonstrations (traces/), the approved pixel
#     baselines (baselines/), and the human sign-off artifacts (signoffs/) that
#     SLICES.json cites as the reason a slice is approved. A trace is the ONE artifact in
#     the system that cannot be regenerated without a human replaying the game.
#
#   .loombridge/tests/  the stamped Unity test results (.loombridge/tests/test-results.xml),
#     their binding manifest (.loombridge/tests/test-results-manifest.json), and the run log
#     (.loombridge/tests/test-run.log). `loombridge tests run` produces them and
#     `loombridge verify` grades them OFFLINE, so committing them is what lets a reviewer, a
#     CI job, or a later verify read the evidence without re-running a multi-minute editor.
#
#   .loombridge/verify/  the captured op output the Tier-1 gates read, and the reason a
#     clone can re-grade an approved slice with no editor at all.
#
#   .loombridge/registry/  imported asset packs. Project INPUTS: re-deriving one may need
#     a hosted catalog a clone or a CI runner cannot reach.
#
# A guard test walks this file against the path constants, so an ignore rule added here
# that contradicts the split fails the suite.

# Legacy: CLIs before the .loombridge/run/backups/ move dropped the update backup here.
ProjectSettings/LoombridgeInstall.json.bak

